f i'm a robot and i don't  know  that's a reference to doombots doombots  are basically robot duplicates of dr  doom that he created to operate in his  stead when he doesn't want to appear in  public the reason why this is important  is because the doombots actually believe  they're dr doom they don't know their  robots so whenever it is the doombots  attack a city or something like that  it's usually only one that ever does it  then the doombot  operates as if they're dr doom it's a  really cool concept  the other reference could simply be to  life model decoys because life model  decoys don't know that they're decoys  they actually believe they're that  particular person and for the fourth  little easter egg that i found i  initially thought the little kid that  owen wilson's character was talking to  was bennett du perry it's not benidoo  perry was born a couple hundred years  before this kid but who has been a  duponte this guy  is a universally powerful telepath and  telekinetic he's also a mutant  yes i will take every chance i can to  speculate on the idea that whatever it  is that i happen to see in the mcu  is somehow going to bring mutants into  the mcu i'm sorry  i'm an x-men fan i will always do that  so having said all that let's talk about  this main villain of the series if i'm  being honest i think this variant  version of loki  is actually a character called ikol yes  it's loki spelled backwards nobody ever  said marvel was imaginative when it came  to names but here's the important thing  when it comes to this with loki's deaths  and resurrections they've happened a lot  over the years the classic version of  loki which is the version with horns and  all that kind of stuff he existed for  years and years and years until you got  to an event that was called  ragnarok you guys have all heard of this  it's also called thor disassembled in  the comics basically over the course of  this loki leaves an attack on asgard  thor is ultimately defeated and he ends  up going on this kind of crazy quest  this leads to him destroying the world  tree by destroying the world tree it  also destroys all the asgardians and  asgard itself  eventually a guy by the name of j  michael cerzinski started writing the  thor comics and when he did he had thor  rebuild asgard and brock's in oklahoma  and then basically started resurrecting  all the asgardians this happened because  the asgardian spirits lived on but they  were placed inside mortal bodies  eventually what happened is that he came  across the body that was supposed to  belong to seth but loki  actually took it and so loki comes back  as a woman now following that you go  into the lady loki storyline which  doesn't last super long and you get this  really really cool story where he  actually impersonates the scarlet witch  but the whole idea of lady loki  eventually goes into a story called  siege on asgard there's a lot of things  that go on none of which you guys really  care about  the important thing is that lady loki or  at least male loki who have been lady  loki at one point  ends up dying this gives birth to a  character named kid loki but then it  also goes into another version named  ikel while kid loki did come after the  events of siege honestly ikol is this  kind of  reincarnated version or the most modern  version of loki but aikol did some  pretty twisted stuff  initially he was just kind of a guy who  was trying to understand why he  sacrificed his life during the events of  siege but  far into the future he's a version of  loki that actually killed all the  superheroes on earth  really killed everybody on earth he  eventually became the all butcher after  taking the sword that belonged to gore  the god butcher who'd used it to kill  all kinds of gods from across the  universe but the question that has to be  asked here is if it really is that  future version of loki the character of  ikol  why is he traveling across the entirety  of the multiverse killing all these  different members of the time variance  authority and stealing their timeline  reset charges  if i'm a vetting man i think there's  only one of two possibilities here the  first  is that this version of ikol is working  for king the conqueror king the  conqueror as we know is going to appear  in ant-man 3. yes i know kevin feige  said the tv shows are not going to be  required viewing in order to understand  what's going on in the movies  but you guys are taking that too  literally it's like comic books yeah  sure there's a main event which is  basically the movies but then there's  also tie-ins are they required to  understand the main story  no do they help yes now if he really is  working for kane the conqueror i don't  think those two things will be connected  until we get to ant-man 3 and we  actually see jonathan majors as kane the  conqueror and if anything i think it'll  just bolster or at least go to show how  wide reaching the influence of king the  conqueror is after all  he rules entire sections of the  multiverse the second idea and the one  that's probably the most probable here  is that that version of loki  is a time twister so the tv show  established the idea that the tva was  created by the time keepers who exist to  basically make sure  that the timeline is maintained the  animation told us the time keepers came  together as a result of the chaotic mess  that was the war that initially started  that led to the entire madness that was  the multiverse at that particular point  in time in order to keep that from  happening the timekeepers condensed the  entire multiverse down to a singular  timeline in order to ensure that when  new alternate realities were created  that it was a controlled process  they couldn't just be done arbitrarily  the time twisters were the first attempt  to create  timekeepers it ended up going awry now i  don't know if it's like it is in the  comics where you have three time  twisters and then you have three time  keepers but i would argue that if this  is the case then that is a time twister  and the idea here is to  set the entire multiverse into madness  or the very least reset the entire  multiverse because we know whoever this  villain is is traveling around killing  off all these different members of the  tva who are investigating divergent  timelines that this person's basically  creating  and then as soon as the tva shows up  they're ambushed they're killed  and then their reset charger is taken  and if you combine enough of those  together it's akin to what gore the  godbutcher was doing in the jason aaron  thor god of thunder story where he was  looking to create a god bomb that he  would send throughout the entire time  stream  and basically kill all the gods across  the entirety of the universe  except imagine that it would just reset  the entirety of the multiverse just like  creating a giant reset button  that's what i think is most likely going  on here but let me know what you guys  think down in the comments section thank  you guys for watching  and i will catch you all later peace

